I'm checking the `entire` installation logic — the curl command could hang if the network is slow or the install script itself doesn't complete, and even if `entire` is already installed, running `entire version` could block indefinitely if the command doesn't respond. But actually, during a reinstall of the same version, the flow skips this entire block and goes straight to `runInit()`, so the hang would only occur when installing a new version.

The real issue is that both the curl install and the version check lack timeouts. I'm thinking the simplest solution would be to add a timeout wrapper around these operations...

